From 8fdd954770f3718ad13bb9dec906f0c9e6fb0bfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:07:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] fix(#95): failing_tests, unscored_records,
 shape_hazards and load_failure are read directly or named absent

The defect, verbatim from the issue: "an object that never carried the flag reads clean." Twelve sites
read these four with a default meaning "no test fails / no mutant went unscored / no hazard / the module
loaded".

Why the obvious fix is wrong: they are two different kinds of reader.
* Where the object is a Wesker `ProfilingResult` (which declares `failing_tests` and `unscored_records`)
  or a `ScopeMap` (which declares `load_failure`) the read is DIRECT: converge._missing_line_standings,
  converge._converge_impl, audit.audit_suite, cli._floor_cause_of, _unscored_flag_refusal, _format_scope,
  _diagnose_action.
* `validity.normalize_validity` is the adapter that takes any engine result, so it is three-valued:
  `shape_hazards`, `unscored_records` and `failing_tests` join `_ADAPTED_FIELDS`, an engine that does not
  report one is recorded `absent:<field>` in `capability_flags`, and the detail derived from it is empty
  because nothing was reported.
* One read was never a fault-flag read at all: `_converge_action` took `shape_hazards` off the
  ConvergeResult, which has no such field (the hazards live on `result.validity`), so the "Affected"
  rows naming the tests that forced isolation were unreachable outside a test double. It now reads the
  validity, and a result built with no validity has no tests to name.

Not closed: the not-consulted / missing-line / write-refused families and the rest of the registry.

FAULT_OPEN failing_tests 4 -> 0, unscored_records 6 -> 0, shape_hazards 2 -> 0, load_failure 3 -> 0.
Disarmed, 3 of the 4 new intent tests fail (the fourth restates behaviour test_measurement_validity covers).
The 34-file neighbour set (693 tests) and the four guards pass under 3.14 and 3.12; ruff clean under
pinned 0.16.7.
